  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.97",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\lambda:=c^{2}_{1}/c_{2}$ be the Chern slope of a closed, almost complex 4–manifold X. What is the supremum of $\\lambda as X$ ranges over the following families?\n\n(a) Symplectic $\\Sigma_{g}–bundles$ over $\\Sigma_{h}$, with g, $h \\geq$ 2.\n\n(b) Holomorphic $\\Sigma_{g}–bundles$ over $\\Sigma_{h}$, with g, $h \\geq$ 2.\n\n(c) Symplectic Lefschetz fibrations over $S^{2}$.\n\n(d) Holomorphic Lefschetz fibrations over $S^{2}$. (Here, the Lefschetz fibrations are assumed to have critical points.)",
    "sha256": "498f1864e0bbba4ce02d3793589cb6ea73d9d34b6b8d021c6333453f1e32e374",
